{"id":"15.5.3","doc":"T","title":"GDMA","words":278,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3's "},{"t":"num","v":"32 MB","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" External SRAM can be independently split into four regions, of which the Region1 and Region2 are accessible to "},{"t":"block","v":"GDMA","id":"gdma"},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 15.5-3. Split the External SRAM into Four Split Regions for GDMA","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Split Regions"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Starting Address (included)"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Ending Address (not included) (2)"}]],"rows":[{"n":2,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Region0 (3)"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x3C000000"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_0_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1,2)"}]]},{"n":3,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Region1 (4)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_0_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_1_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1,2)"}]]},{"n":4,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Region2 (4)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_1_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_2_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1,2)"}]]},{"n":5,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Region3 (3)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_EDMA_BOUNDARY_2_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" (1)"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x3E000000 (2)"}]]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"1 When configuring this register, note that you need to write an offset to 0x3C000000 and the unit is "},{"t":"num","v":"4 KB","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For example, configuring the register to 0x80 means that the address is 0x3C000000 + 0x80 * "},{"t":"num","v":"4 KB","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" = 0x3C080000. 2 The address value filled here is the Ending address plus one. For example, 0x3E000000 means that the end address is 0x3DFFFFFF. 3 This region cannot be accessed by peripherals via GDMA. 4 This region can be accessed by some peripherals via GDMA, including "},{"t":"block","v":"SPI2","id":"spi"},{"t":"text","v":", SPI3, UHCI0, "},{